        "original_id": "7b63f2c8-f0e8-5515-9bc3-3a5a99d6e50f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Edna St. Vincent Millay, Robert Penn Warren\n- Works: \"Renascence\", All the King's Men, At Heaven's Gate\n- Awards: Pulitzer Prize for Poetry, Pulitzer Prize for the Novel\n- Topics: feminist activism\n\nFacts:\n- In 1912, Edna St. Vincent Millay wrote the poem \"Renascence,\" also spelled \"Renasance.\"\n- \"Renascence\" is often considered one of Edna St. Vincent Millay's finest poems and is credited with introducing Edna St. Vincent Millay to a wider audience.\n- In 1923, Edna St. Vincent Millay received the Pulitzer Prize for Poetry and became the third woman to win the award for poetry.\n- Edna St. Vincent Millay was also known for feminist activism.\n- In 1946, Robert Penn Warren published the novel All the King's Men.\n- At Heaven's Gate is the second novel by Robert Penn Warren.\n- In 1947, Robert Penn Warren received the Pulitzer Prize for the Novel for All the King's Men.\n- In 1958 and 1979, Robert Penn Warren received the Pulitzer Prize for Poetry.\n- Robert Penn Warren is the only person to have won Pulitzer Prizes for both fiction and poetry.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "09511dfb-45ed-5b89-bfda-85eea3505304",
        "text": "Page: Edna St. Vincent Millay. Sentence: She received the Pulitzer Prize for Poetry in 1923, the third woman to win the award for poetry, and was also known for her feminist activism.\nPage: Robert Penn Warren. Sentence: He received the 1947 Pulitzer Prize for the Novel for his novel \"All the King's Men\" (1946) and the Pulitzer Prize for Poetry in 1958 and 1979.\nPage: Robert Penn Warren. Sentence: He is the only person to have won Pulitzer Prizes for both fiction and poetry.\nPage: Renascence (poem). Sentence: \"Renascence\" (also \"Renasance\") is a 1912 poem by Edna St. Vincent Millay, credited with introducing her to the wider world, and often considered one of her finest poems.\nPage: At Heaven's Gate. Sentence: At Heaven's Gate is the second novel by Robert Penn Warren.",
